# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Static export can't emit a next.config headers() block, so
# the baseline security headers live here and apply to every path: clickjacking, MIME sniffing,
# referrer leakage, and a hash-based Content-Security-Policy.
#
# The CSP is generated after the build by scripts/gen-csp.mjs, which replaces the CSP-PLACEHOLDER
# line below with a policy whose script-src lists the SHA-256 of every inline script the static
# export emits (the pre-paint theme-init script, the JSON-LD block, and Next's per-page hydration
# scripts). Static export has no request-time nonce, and the hashes are computed from the exact
# bytes served, so the policy always matches the page. connect-src 'self' also enforces the
# "no third-party requests / nothing uploaded" property the app's privacy copy promises.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Lock down powerful APIs the calculator never uses, and isolate the browsing context.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  # CSP-PLACEHOLDER

# Ask caches to revalidate the service worker so a new deploy is detected promptly. NOTE:
# Cloudflare Pages currently serves /sw.js with its own multi-hour max-age regardless of this
# rule, so prompt update detection is actually guaranteed by registering the worker with
# updateViaCache: "none" (components/ServiceWorker.tsx), which fetches sw.js past the HTTP cache
# on every update check. This rule states the intent and takes effect if that override is lifted.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
